TI  - Anatomical considerations in bronchoscopy.
PG  - S1123-S1127
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.08.116 [doi]
AB  - A thorough understanding of intrathoracic anatomy enables the interventional 
      bronchoscopist to perform procedures efficaciously. The review of the anatomy of 
      the thoracic cavity focuses first on the trachea and the relationship of the 
      airway with surrounding structures, knowledge important for the safe conduct of 
      bronchoscopic procedures. We then describe the anatomy of the pleural cavity 
      relevant to the practitioner performing pleuroscopy.
