AB  - Pleural procedures are commonly performed by physicians from a range of 
      specialities. These procedures vary in complexity, from relatively 
      straightforward pleural aspiration to more challenging procedures such as 
      pleuroscopy. After appropriate training, even complex pleural procedures have a 
      low risk of complications. Nevertheless, an appreciation of procedural risks is 
      essential for physician training and forms the crux of a valid patient consent 
      process. This review presents a systematic evaluation of the potential 
      complications of common pleural procedures.
