TI  - Sago-grain nodules in tubercular pleural effusion.
PG  - 3750-3751
LID - 10.1002/ppul.27186 [doi]
AB  - A 6-year-old boy was referred with complaints of chest pain for 2 months with 
      low-grade fever. A computerized tomography of the chest revealed a loculated 
      pleural effusion on the left side. Medical thoracoscopy was performed that 
      revealed a characteristic sago-grain follicle over the parietal pleural. 
      Histopathology and microbiological investigations on pleural biopsy samples 
      confirmed tubercular pleural effusion.
