TI  - Rigid and semirigid pleuroscopy: the future is bright.
PG  - 418-25
AB  - Pleuroscopy provides the pulmonologist with a unique opportunity to visualize the 
      contents of the pleural space, perform biopsy of the parietal pleura under direct 
      visual guidance, allow optimal chest tube placement and perform pleurodesis to 
      prevent recurrent pleural effusion or pneumothorax in selected patients. We 
      discuss the techniques, indications, contraindications and complications of 
      pleuroscopy using rigid and semirigid instruments. In addition, the potential 
      value and expanding role of pleuroscopy with semirigid instrumentation is 
      debated.
