TI  - [Medical thoracoscopy in the elucidationof recurrent pleural effusion].
LID - V08190443 [pii]
AB  - Medical thoracoscopy allows the respiratory physician access to inspection and 
      biopsy of the pleura. The method has several names, such as pleuroscopy, 
      non-intubated thoracoscopy and exploratory thoracoscopy, all of which cover the 
      same procedure. The main indication for medical thoracoscopy is the diagnosis of 
      recurrent pleural effusion, where pleural biopsy is needed. Medical thoracoscopy 
      differs from thoracic surgical surgery as patients are sedated rather than in 
      general anaesthesia. This is a review of the state of the art of pulmonological 
      investigations of recurrent pleural effusion and the important role of medical 
      thoracoscopy.
