TI  - Eosinophilic Pleural Effusion as an Unusual Initial Manifestation of IgG4-Related 
      Disease: A Diagnostic Challenge.
PG  - e91102
LID - 10.7759/cureus.91102 [doi]
LID - e91102
AB  - We report the case of a 79-year-old male who presented with progressive dyspnea 
      over the course of one month. Chest radiography revealed a left-sided pleural 
      effusion. Pleural fluid analysis demonstrated an exudative profile with 
      eosinophil-predominant cytology. Medical thoracoscopy identified multiple 
      hyperpigmented spots on the anterior parietal pleura. Histopathological 
      examination of pleural biopsy specimens confirmed the diagnosis of IgG4-related 
      disease (IgG4-RD). The pleural effusion resolved completely following 
      corticosteroid therapy.
