TI  - [Hodgkin's disease limited to intrathoracic sites. Case report].
PG  - 614-6
AB  - Hodgkin's disease without peripheral lymphadenopathy or hepatosplenomegaly is 
      exceptional. CASE REPORT: Hodgkin's disease was revealed by lung nodules, one of 
      them cavitating, with mediastinal enlargement. Diagnosis was confirmed on a 
      video-assisted pleuroscopic biopsy. CONCLUSION: Hodgkin's disease should be 
      considered in case of mediastinal enlargement with lung nodules.
